    o = ["# Task B report: field extraction / document understanding", "",
         "> **Task B is a research prototype, not a production OCR service.** Generated by `scripts/taskB/make_report.py` from `reports/taskB/*.json` and `models/taskB/hybrid.json`. Real-document results are the headline; synthetic results are always reported separately and are **not** evidence of real-world generalisation.", "",
         "## 1. Objective", "Input: one bill page (image or PDF page), its OCR words and bounding boxes. Output: structured JSON with, per field, value, calibrated confidence (null when no calibrated score exists), model score, source system and bbox. A field the document does not contain is **omitted (null)**; nothing is guessed. Task A (classification) is untouched; Task B reuses its manifest, OCR annotations, group-based splits and image conventions.", "",
         "## 2. Canonical schema", "34 fields in six groups (`models/taskB/field_schema.json`): universal (" + ", ".join(GROUPS["universal"]) + "); Indian tax (" + ", ".join(GROUPS["indian_tax"]) + "); employee (" + ", ".join(GROUPS["employee"]) + "); travel (" + ", ".join(GROUPS["travel"]) + "); hotel (" + ", ".join(GROUPS["hotel"]) + "); medical (" + ", ".join(GROUPS["medical"]) + "). Normalisation (`schema.py`): amounts -> float (default `1,234.50`, EU `6,14`, Indonesian thousands-only); dates -> ISO; GSTIN -> 15-char pattern (+ checksum helper, OCR digit/letter repair); ids/text -> alnum-casefold; places -> city part. Source -> canonical mapping and unsupported source fields: `reports/taskB/schema_mapping.md`.", "",
         "## 3. Dataset composition", f"Task B documents: **{sm['total_docs']}**; **real {sm['real']}**, **synthetic {sm['synthetic']}**, Indian real {sm['indian_real']}. Splits (existing group-based manifest split, unchanged): {sm['by_split']}; `synthetic_b` (1,080 Task-B-only synthetic bills for fields no real data annotates) uses a seeded document-level split. Sources: {sm['by_source']}. A field is scored on a document only if its source annotates it (absence is then meaningful).", "",
         "**Ground-truth correction applied once, to all splits, before the final numbers below.** ReceiptBench stores `std_total = '0.00'` as a placeholder when unknown while `orig_total` holds the printed total. The first mapping read only `std_total`, so 182 documents (27 in the real test set) were scored against a wrong zero. Now `total_amount` uses `std_total`, else `orig_total`; 88 totals were recovered, 94 documents with neither are **not scored** for total_amount. No other label or split was changed. Effect on the same models: real micro-F1 hybrid " + f3(micro(fb['by_system']['hybrid']['test']['real'], list(fb['by_system']['hybrid']['test']['real']))['f1']) + " -> " + f3(mf('hybrid', 'real')['f1']) + ", LayoutLMv3 " + f3(micro(fb['by_system']['layoutlm']['test']['real'], list(fb['by_system']['layoutlm']['test']['real']))['f1']) + " -> " + f3(mf('layoutlm', 'real')['f1']) + " (`final_results_before_gt_fix.json` keeps the old run). The candidate ranker was retrained on corrected labels (cheap); LayoutLMv3 was **not** retrained (its token labels differed only on those documents, mostly missing rather than wrong).", "",
         "### Annotation audit", "", "| Field | Total | Real | Synthetic | Indian real | Located in OCR | Sources |", "|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|"]
    for f, a in au["fields"].items(): o.append(f"| {f} | {a['total']} | {a['real']} | {a['synthetic']} | {a['indian_real']} | {a['aligned']} | {', '.join(f'{k}:{v}' for k, v in a['sources'].items()) or '-'} |")
    o += ["", "## 4. Indian-real coverage (explicit)", "", "Real Indian annotated documents (`country == IN`, not synthetic) per split:", "", "| Field | train | val | test | total | verdict |", "|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|"]
    for f in ["gstin", "cgst", "sgst", "igst", "hsn_sac", "merchant_name", "invoice_number", "invoice_date", "total_amount", "subtotal", "tax_total", "merchant_address"]:
        c = [sum(f in d["fields"] for d in X if (not d["synthetic"]) and d["country"] == "IN") for X in (tr, va, te)]; t = sum(c)
        verdict = "NONE: no real Indian annotation exists; real accuracy is unknown" if t == 0 else ("INSUFFICIENT test support (<10): no claim possible" if c[2] < 10 else ("thin test support (<30): indicative only" if c[2] < 30 else "usable"))
        o.append(f"| {f} | {c[0]} | {c[1]} | {c[2]} | {t} | {verdict} |")
    o += ["", "All real Indian field annotation comes from one source (ReceiptBench); **HSN/SAC has no real annotation at all, IGST exactly one real document, subtotal/tax_total/address none for Indian bills**. Where the table says INSUFFICIENT/NONE, synthetic scores are not substituted for evidence. Section 11 adds a 5-fold group cross-validation of the ranker over all real documents for GSTIN/CGST/SGST.", "",
          "## 5. Baseline (deterministic)", "Regex + keyword + position heuristics over OCR words/boxes (`baseline.py`): no learning, no per-dataset tuning, generic bill vocabulary only, crude locale/currency inference, year-like numbers excluded from amounts. Its hotel/travel/medical/employee patterns use label words that the `synthetic_b` templates share, so its synthetic scores are optimistic.", "",
          "## 6. Candidate ranker", "Candidate generation (amounts, dates, 15-char tokens, id-like tokens and 2-3 word windows, text lines/':' suffixes/line windows) + one gradient-boosted classifier per field (value, position, line shape, hashed left/previous/next-line context); CPU only. Decision = best candidate per field, abstain below the field threshold; confidence = isotonic calibration.", "",
          "Candidate-generation vs ranking on REAL test documents (GT present):", "", "| Field | GT docs | GT among candidates | ranked first |", "|---|---:|---:|---:|"]
    for f, v in fr["ranker_candidate_analysis_real_test"].items():
        if v["n_gt"] >= 15: o.append(f"| {f} | {v['n_gt']} | {v['gt_in_candidates']} ({v['gt_in_candidates']/v['n_gt']:.0%}) | {v['top1_correct']} ({v['top1_correct']/v['n_gt']:.0%}) |")
    o += ["", "Reading: for merchant_name and invoice_number the ranker's candidate generator often never produces the right value (candidate-generation failure), whereas for amounts/dates most errors are ranking errors.", "",
          "## 7. LayoutLMv3", "`microsoft/layoutlmv3-base` token classification, BIO tags for all 34 fields over OCR words + boxes + page image; 384-subtoken sliding windows (stride 96); micro-batch 2 x accumulation 8, bf16, up to 5 epochs with early stopping on validation token-F1 (RTX 4050, 6 GB, ~45 min). Training log: " + "; ".join(l.replace("'", "") for l in (R / "ie_layoutlm.log").read_text().splitlines() if l.startswith("{'epoch'")) + ". Decoding: contiguous B-/I- spans plus a best-B fallback; value normalised per field. Weights are CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (non-commercial).", "",
          "## 8. Final system", "**Hybrid + applicability gating.** Per field, one system (LayoutLMv3 / ranker / baseline) is used. Choice and thresholds follow a fixed policy that never touches the test set:", "",
          f"* A field's score threshold and system are **tuned on REAL validation documents only if >= {hy['policy']['MIN_REAL_VAL']} real validation documents carry a GT value for it**; otherwise a fixed untuned default is used (threshold {hy['policy']['DEFAULT_TAU']}, system `{hy['default_system']}` = best real-validation micro-F1 over the well-supported fields: " + ", ".join(f"{k} {v:.3f}" for k, v in fr["default_system_real_val_micro_f1"].items()) + ") and the field is flagged **LOW-SUPPORT**.",
          f"* Confidence = isotonic regression of 'prediction correct' on the model score, fit on real validation predictions when >= {hy['policy']['MIN_REAL_CAL']} exist (else all validation predictions, flagged).",
          "* Gating (`gating.py`): hotel/travel/medical/employee/HSN/tax-part fields are emitted only if the document text contains evidence words. `tax_total` is derived from IGST only for IGST-only bills (annotation convention); `currency` comes from the baseline (symbol rules).", "",
          "| Field | system | threshold | basis | real val GT | calibration |", "|---|---|---:|---|---:|---|"]
    for f, v in ci_.items():
        tinfo = (hy["layoutlm_tau_info"] or {}).get(f) if v["system"] == "layoutlm" else (hy["ranker_tau_info"].get(f) if v["system"] == "ranker" else None)
        if v["real_val_gt"] > 0 or v["system"] != hy["default_system"]:
            o.append(f"| {f} | {v['system']} | {f2(tinfo['tau']) if tinfo else '-'} | {'**LOW-SUPPORT default**' if v['low_support'] else 'real-val tuned'} | {v['real_val_gt']} | {(tinfo or {}).get('calibration', '-')[:60]} |")
    o += ["", "Fields with no real validation documents at all (synthetic-only fields): " + ", ".join(f for f, v in ci_.items() if v["real_val_gt"] == 0) + ". They use the default system/threshold and can be evaluated on synthetic bills only.", "",
          "## 9. Evaluation methodology", "Same held-out test set for every system (`final_eval.py`; test is scored once per system, never used for tuning). Per field: support (docs with GT), precision, recall, F1 with TP = predicted and equal to GT, FP = predicted and (different or GT absent), FN = GT present and (missing or different). **Normalised match**: amounts within 0.005, ISO dates, normalised GSTIN, alnum-casefold text/ids; **soft match** for text/place (0.9 similarity or containment) reported separately; **exact raw match** = raw OCR string equals raw GT string (text/id/GSTIN fields only; amounts/dates have no meaningful raw form). **Null rate** = share of scored documents with no prediction; **hallucination rate** = share of documents where the field is annotated as absent but a value was emitted. Micro-F1 pools TP/FP/FN over fields; macro-F1 averages per-field F1 for fields with >= 5 GT documents. Intervals: grouped bootstrap over real test documents (400 resamples; groups = near-duplicate/template families).", "",
          "## 10. Real test results (held-out real documents)", "", "| System | real micro-F1 (95% CI) | real macro-F1 | Indian-real micro-F1 | micro-F1 on documents scored |", "|---|---:|---:|---:|---|"]
    for s in ALL:
        m = T(s, "real"); o.append(f"| {s}{' (FINAL)' if s == 'hybrid' else ''} | {f3(micro(m, list(m))['f1'])} ({ci[s][0]}-{ci[s][1]}) | {f3(macro(m, list(m)))} | {f3(micro(T(s, 'real_indian'), list(T(s, 'real_indian')))['f1'])} | P {f3(micro(m, list(m))['precision'])} / R {f3(micro(m, list(m))['recall'])} |")
    o += ["", "Paired differences of real micro-F1 (grouped bootstrap 95% CI; 'significant' = interval excludes 0): " + "; ".join(f"**{k}**: {v['ci']} ({'significant' if v['significant'] else 'not significant'})" for k, v in pd_.items()) + ".", "",
          "**Does LayoutLMv3 improve over the simpler systems?** Yes, on real documents: " + f"LayoutLMv3 {f3(micro(T('layoutlm','real'), list(T('layoutlm','real')))['f1'])} vs ranker {f3(micro(T('ranker','real'), list(T('ranker','real')))['f1'])} vs baseline {f3(micro(T('baseline','real'), list(T('baseline','real')))['f1'])}; both paired differences exclude zero. The hybrid adds a small but significant gain over LayoutLMv3 alone (it keeps the ranker for subtotal and travel_date, where the ranker scored better on real validation). This is unlike Task A, where text alone was enough.", "",
          "### 10.1 Per-field results on REAL test documents (all systems)", "", "| Field | support (real docs with GT) | " + " | ".join(f"{s} F1" for s in ALL) + " | hybrid P | hybrid R | hybrid exact-raw | hybrid null rate | hybrid halluc. rate (n absent) |", "|---|---:|" + "---:|" * len(ALL) + "---:|---:|---:|---:|---|"]
